 ## Overview
-Dynamic Scene and Temporal Modeling extends the static Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) architecture to handle scenes that change over time, solving the problem of rendering temporal variations in geometry and appearance that vanilla NeRF cannot represent [15546-dynamic-scene-and-temporal-modeling.md]. These methods differ from their siblings by explicitly incorporating time as a dimension, modeling deformation fields, or stratifying the scene based on motion scales, rather than treating the scene as a static 5D function [15546-dynamic-scene-and-temporal-modeling.md].
